WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.652
The module is organized into four parts, and the order matters.

00:00:04.652 --> 00:00:06.962
Part 1 is the core build.

00:00:06.962 --> 00:00:14.857
We create a complete working RAG pipeline ourselves with Python, NumPy, and Sentence Transformers.

00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:18.377
This gives us a transparent baseline.

00:00:18.377 --> 00:00:18.912
Part 2 is storage.

00:00:18.912 --> 00:00:26.222
Once the baseline works, we move the vectors into Chroma and then compare other vector-search options.

00:00:26.222 --> 00:00:33.816
The point is to see that changing the storage layer does not require changing the whole application.

00:00:34.509 --> 00:00:37.432
Part 3 focuses on retrieval quality.

00:00:37.432 --> 00:00:45.602
We introduce metadata filters, top-k, BM25, hybrid retrieval, reranking, and query rewriting.

00:00:45.602 --> 00:00:48.192
Part 4 is evaluation and production thinking.

00:00:48.192 --> 00:00:54.912
We measure retrieval, diagnose failures, think about security and freshness,

00:00:54.912 --> 00:01:01.522
and connect the classroom system to the architecture companies use.

00:01:01.522 --> 00:01:06.018
If Part 1 is clear, the rest of the module becomes much easier.
